        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-05-07T18:41:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Blackfang108\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Blackfang108:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How so?&nbsp;Gnocchi literaly translates as \"dumplings.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not exactly.&nbsp; It's translated as \"dumplings\" because that's what the general consensus is that they are.&nbsp; It literally means \"lump\" or \"knot\" (as in wood).</p>",
